# No code debt

This product is in active UI and foundation build. Do not accumulate transitional leftovers.

## Hard rules

1. When replacing a UI pattern, **delete the old implementation in the same change**. Do not keep the previous layout "just in case," behind a flag, or commented out.
2. Do not add `// TODO: remove`, unused props, dead CSS classes, duplicate components, or parallel "v1/v2" files for the same screen.
3. If a helper only served the deleted UI, remove it or rewrite it for the new UI — no orphan helpers.
4. Prefer one clear path: one component, one layout, one state model per screen responsibility.
5. Temporary scaffolding is allowed only when it ships in the same PR that deletes it, or is explicitly time-boxed and removed before merge.

## Review check

Before finishing a UI change, ask: *If I delete the old code now, does anything break?* If no — delete it now.
